eed and head start distance.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the Head Start Distance\n\nThe first train leaves at **9:40** and the second train leaves at **10:15**.\n\nFirst, calculate the time difference between their departures:\n$$10:15 - 9:40 = 35 \\text{ minutes}$$\n\nConvert this time into hours to match the speed units (km/h):\n$$35 \\text{ minutes} = \\frac{35}{60} \\text{ hours} = \\frac{7}{12} \\text{ hours}$$\n\nDuring this 35-minute gap, the first train travels at $72 \\text{ km/h}$. Calculate the distance it covers:\n$$d_{\\text{head start}} = \\text{Speed}_1 \\times \\text{Time}_{\\text{gap}}$$\n$$d_{\\text{head start}} = 72 \\text{ km/h} \\times \\frac{7}{12} \\text{ h", "client": {"ttft_s": 0.8715047000005143, "decode_s": 4.309894500001974, "total_s": 5.1817210000008345, "n_gen": 256, "n_chunks": 256, "tg": 59.166181445945654, "pp": 73.43620751553289}}
